  "verbalization": "Sisomicin is shown to have a direct target relationship with the CD276 antigen through multiple pathways, all leading to the same target cell line, RPMI-7951. The drug is implicated in inhibiting the CD276 antigen through the action of various compounds, including (1S,3R,5S,8S,9R,12R,13S,14R)-14-hydroxy-13-methyl-14-propan-2-yl-4,7,10-trioxapentacyclo[6.4.1.19,12.03,5.05,13]tetradecane-6,11-dione and 3-[7-methoxy-5-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-1-benzofuran-6-yl]propanoic acid, which are both known to target the CD276 antigen. These findings suggest that Sisomicin may exert its effect by modulating the expression or activity of the CD276 antigen, potentially through a common mechanism involving the inhibition of a shared target in RPMI-7951. The consistent targeting of the same cell line across different compounds supports a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be elucidated. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected biological role of CD276 in immune regulation, making the relationship between Sisomicin and CD276 antigen a promising candidate for further investigation.",
